  "_style": "Write warm everyday Javanese in ngoko alus, Latin script only (no Aksara Jawa), using standard spelling with dh/th (dhewe, thukul, kutha) and plain e, no diacritics like é or è. Address the user as “panjenengan” (possessive after the noun: “taman panjenengan”), never kowe/sampeyan/kamu; keep verbs in plain ngoko (nulis, ngirim, nandur) and avoid heavy krama that sounds stiff in an app. The couple together is “panjenengan sakloron” (never the Indonesian “berdua”); “we/our” from the couple’s point of view is “kita” (“Wit kita”). The other person is always “pasangan” / “pasangan panjenengan” (never bojo, garwa, pacar, mas/mbak, dheweke for the partner when the name or “pasangan” fits); Javanese pronouns are gender-neutral, so keep sentences free of gendered words like lanang/wadon/mas/mbak. A partner’s name placeholder (%@) is never changed, affixed or declined (no “%@-e”, no “%@-ne”): rephrase instead, e.g. “pasangan panjenengan, %@,” or “saka %@”. Quotes: curly double “ ” outside, single ‘ ’ inside; ellipsis is the single character …; no space before ? ! : ; and one space after; keep emoji, the “ · ” separator, \\n and all placeholders exactly as in the source. Numbers use a dot for thousands and a comma for decimals (1.250; 4,5); dates are day month year with Javanese/Indonesian month names written as in Indonesian (14 November 2026), time in 24-hour form (21.30 or 21:30 as the system formats it). Buttons are short imperatives without “mangga/monggo/tulung” (Simpen, Kirim layang, Coba maneh); titles, tabs, chips and buttons use sentence case (only the first letter capitalised), except proper names such as Coupley, Premium, AI. Plural category is only “other”: Javanese nouns do not inflect for number, so write “%lld dina” for every count (no reduplication after a number). Tone: warm, light, kind and natural, never cheesy, never literal word-for-word; prefer common Javanese words over Indonesian ones, but keep familiar loanwords (aplikasi, notifikasi, widget, kuis, akun) where Javanese has no everyday equivalent.",
